The phase accumulator in `aggregateJobMetrics` silently drops every interval that is still open when an event stream ends, and the native engine can never re-enter the `running` phase after a settle. Both were re-derived by the coordinator against CURRENT master `<redacted>` (not inherited from the N3 evidence base, which was measured on the superseded tree `feature/xtrm-93-n0n2-recon` @ `553b5a23`).

DEFECT 1 - NO POST-LOOP FLUSH. In `src/specialist/observability-sqlite.ts` the accumulator is
    :2992  let activeRuntimeMs = 0;
    :2993  let waitingMs = 0;
    :2994  let phase: 'running' | 'waiting' | null = null;
    :2995  let phaseStartedAtMs: number | null = null;
    :2997  const closePhase = (endAtMs: number): void => { ... }
`closePhase` has EXACTLY THREE call sites and all three are inside the event loop (`for (const event of events)` opens at :3007): :3036 (`status_change` to running/waiting), :3042 (`status_change` to done/error/cancelled) and :3050 (`run_complete`). After the loop the code back-fills
    :3065  if (startedAtMs !== null && completedAtMs === null) { completedAtMs = events.length > 0 ? events[events.length - 1]!.t : startedAtMs; }
    :3068  if (elapsedMs === null && startedAtMs !== null && completedAtMs !== null) { elapsedMs = Math.max(0, completedAtMs - startedAtMs); }
which feeds `completed_at_ms` and `elapsed_ms` ONLY. It does NOT call `closePhase`. Therefore any phase still open at end-of-stream is subtracted from BOTH `active_runtime_ms` and `waiting_ms`, with no error, no log line and no null column.

DEFECT 2 - NO RUNNING RE-ENTRY EDGE ON THE NATIVE PATH. `src/specialist/native-activation-observability.ts:317-318` maps `activation_settled` to `createStatusChangeEvent('waiting', 'running')`, which closes the running phase and opens a waiting phase. Searching every `createStatusChangeEvent` call site in `src/`, the ONLY producer of a `running` status is `src/specialist/supervisor.ts:1865` - the LEGACY engine. The native mapper emits exactly one `status_change` and it is `waiting`. `activation_resumed` has no case arm in `mapNativeLifecycleEvent` and falls to `default: return null` (:~470). Its recorded rationale in `NATIVE_LIFECYCLE_OBSERVABILITY_GAPS` (:57) is "the resumed run re-enters the shared stream at turn_start" - but the loop's `turn_summary` branch (:3016-3021) and `token_usage` branch (:3023-3026) both `continue` WITHOUT touching `phase`. So re-entering at `turn_start` does NOT re-enter the `running` phase. Every second of a resumed native leg is therefore attributed to `waiting_ms`, and `active_runtime_ms` under-counts by the same amount.

WHY THIS MATTERS MORE THAN THE BUG. The N3 brief's own acceptance check for this node - "active_runtime_ms and waiting_ms sum to no MORE than wall clock, and active_runtime_ms is not under-counted" - is SATISFIED BY THE DEFECT. Dropping intervals can only make the sum smaller. A regression written to that check passes against the broken implementation. The parent epic SPECIALISTS-94 corrected this at contract revision 3; this node inherits the corrected form.

SCOPE-BOUNDARY FACT THE COORDINATOR MEASURED, so it is not assumed: `specialist_job_metrics` currently contains 2827 rows and ZERO of them carry an `act:` job_id, while `specialist_forensic_events` holds 96763 `act:` rows across 267 activations. `aggregateJobMetrics` has no caller anywhere in `src/activation/`; its callers are `src/specialist/supervisor.ts:1073` (legacy, via `aggregateJobMetricsBestEffort`), `src/cli/control.ts:139,146` (legacy), `src/cli/db.ts:550`, and the retention/extract path at `src/specialist/observability-sqlite.ts:3320` which iterates stale rows of the LEGACY `specialist_events` table. So the defect is REAL and its fix is REAL, but its present-day observable effect is on legacy rows. Do NOT write a test that asserts native phase accounting while native cannot reach the projection - that is the false-green shape this programme exists to eliminate. Determine and REPORT the reachability; do not silently assume either answer.

